; r8-ptr-select.spvasm -- lane-r8downgrade fixture (R8 downgrade census, arm C).
; A physically-addressed module whose only physical-addressing feature is
; an OpSelect over two pointer values, with NO VariablePointers /
; VariablePointersStorageBuffer capability declared: the physical model
; grants pointer value flow implicitly, but under the Logical model
; spirv-val rejects it ("Using pointers with OpSelect requires capability
; VariablePointers or VariablePointersStorageBuffer"). R8 must decline by
; name and leave the module physical. (With either capability declared
; the shape stays legal after the downgrade and R8 still strips -- see
; the control cases in spirvfix-r8.test.mjs.)
OpCapability Shader
OpCapability PhysicalStorageBufferAddresses
OpExtension "SPV_KHR_physical_storage_buffer"
OpMemoryModel PhysicalStorageBuffer64 GLSL450
OpEntryPoint Vertex %main "main" %pos %pos2
OpDecorate %pos Location 0
OpDecorate %pos2 Location 1
%void = OpTypeVoid
%f32 = OpTypeFloat 32
%v4 = OpTypeVector %f32 4
%bool = OpTypeBool
%ptr_out_v4 = OpTypePointer Output %v4
%fn = OpTypeFunction %void
%one = OpConstant %f32 1.0
%posval = OpConstantComposite %v4 %one %one %one %one
%t = OpConstantTrue %bool
%pos = OpVariable %ptr_out_v4 Output
%pos2 = OpVariable %ptr_out_v4 Output
%main = OpFunction %void None %fn
%ml = OpLabel
%sel = OpSelect %ptr_out_v4 %t %pos %pos2
OpStore %sel %posval
OpReturn
OpFunctionEnd
